   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to removing the option to file an opportunity to ballot\npetition in the June 2021 primary election; and providing for the repeal of\nsuch provisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S4381",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4381-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Elections",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4381\n\nSPONSOR: RAMOS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to removing the option to file an opportunity to\nballot petition in the June 2021 primary election; and providing for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to remove the option to file an opportunity\nto ballot petition in the June 2021 primary election.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 provides that notwithstanding section 6-164 of the Election\nLaw, there shall be no option to file an opportunity to ballot petition\nin the June 2021 primary election.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe state of emergency caused by the coronavirus pandemic necessitates a\nlimitation on petitioning activities related to the June 2021 primary\nelection. To ensure safety during the political process and to allow for\na more truncated political calendar, this bill removes the option to\nfile opportunity to ballot petitions in the June 2021 primary election.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  New bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNot yet determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed December 31, 2021.\n",
